          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em universal Vassiliev invariant
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vassiliev+knot+invariant"} Vassiliev knot invariant
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+power+series"} formal power series
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+diagrams"} Jacobi diagrams
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck%27s+constant"} Planck's constant
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℏ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hbar
            whose leading term in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℏ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hbar
            on a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+knot"} singular knot
            is its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chord+diagram"} chord diagram
          %p
            By evaluating (framed)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weight+systems"} weight systems
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+diagram"} Jacobi diagram
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            of a universal Vassiliev invariant it defines a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            from framed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weight+systems"} weight systems
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+diagrams"} Jacobi diagrams
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chord+diagrams+modulo+4T+are+Jacobi+diagrams+modulo+STU"} equivalently
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/round+chord+diagrams"} round chord diagrams
            to actual (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"}> ground field
            \-valued)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vassiliev+knot+invariants"} Vassiliev knot invariants
          %p
            This construction in particular yields the proof that
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weight+systems+are+the+associated+graded+objects+of+Vassiliev+invariants"} weight systems are the associated graded objects of Vassiliev invariants
          %p
            In principle there is a vector space of universal Vassiliev invariants, but all that appear in the literature tend to agree (
            %a{:href => "#BNGRT97"}> BNGRT 97
            ) and are identified (
            %a{:href => "#AF96"}> AF 96
            ) with the un-traced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+loop+observable"} Wilson loop observable
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantization+of+3d+Chern-Simons+theory"} perturbative Chern-Simons theory
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/UniversalWilsonLoopObservable.jpg", :width => "700"}/
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/TheGrandStoryOfVassilievKnotInvariantsII.jpg", :width => "800"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Differential+Cohomotopy+implies+intersecting+brane+observables"} Sati-Schreiber 19c
          %p
            The main other known universal Vassiliev iunvariant is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kontsevich+integral"} Kontsevich integral
            (see
            %a{:href => "#Lescop02"} Lescop 02
            for the comparison).
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#Ingredients Ingredients
          %p Write
          #eq:CSFeynmanDiagrams.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mi cs
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{D}^{cs} \;\in\; Set^{\mathbb{N}}
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+set"} graded set
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
            of trivalent framed knot graphs –
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+diagrams"} Feynman diagrams
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            in the presence of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+loops"} Wilson loops
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#AF96"} AF 96, Section 1
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#CattaneoCottaRamusinoLongoni02"} CCRL 02
          %p
            By definition, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph"} graph
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mi cs
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \in \mathcal{D}^{cs}
            must have
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/even+number"} even number
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertices"} vertices
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#AF96"} AF 96, (2.9)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo #
                      %msub
                        %mi Vert
                        %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                    %mi cs
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Gamma \;\in\; \mathcal{D}^{cs}_{(\# Vert_\Gamma)/2}
                  \\,.
          %p
            For any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mi cs
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \in \mathcal{D}^{cs}
            write
